type: dataset
title: 西醫舉隅 / Xi yi ju yu [Gleanings of Western medicine]
version: 0.3.0
authors:
- family-names: Chu
  given-names: Chen-Yu
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9738-6914
url: https://github.com/poplolioi11/bodleian-sinica1842-xiyi-juyu-1875
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: Xi yi ju yu [Gleanings of Western medicine] is an 1875 compilation of John Dudgeon’s medical
  articles from Zhong xi wen jian lu, catalogued with the place [Peking] and held as Bodleian Sinica 1842.
  Its five prefaces and articles on the heart, circulation, eyes and forensic medicine support studies
  of late Qing medicine, translation, visual knowledge and publishing. This release retains 25 source-revised
  frontmatter faces and adds initial transcriptions of 28 complete prose faces and 13 selected diagram-label
  or table layers. JSON, TXT and TEI provide the text, notes, uncertainties and source references; existing
  periodical texts are linked rather than copied. This is a partial-book, AI-assisted edition, without
  full human collation; uncertain readings are marked.
